# Every Python script here starts with `#!/usr/bin/env python3`, and these files are
# meant to be copied out of this repo into other people's projects - including WSL
# and Linux checkouts.
#
# A shebang line ending in CRLF makes the kernel look for an interpreter named
# "python3\r", which fails as `bad interpreter: python3^M`. Cloning on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true is enough to cause it.
#
# Setting it here rather than relying on contributors' local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
